��i<?php exit; ?>a:2:{s:7:"content";O:8:"stdClass":24:{s:2:"ID";i:5350;s:11:"post_author";s:1:"1";s:9:"post_date";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:01";s:13:"post_date_gmt";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:01";s:12:"post_content";s:1214:"<h2 class="blog-details__h2">From theory to shipped software</h2><figure class="blog-details__figure wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://nsc.test/wp-content/themes/NSC-Software/frontend/build/img/blog4.webp" alt="Mentoring Junior Engineers in Distributed Teams — delivery context" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="675" /></figure><blockquote class="blog-details__blockquote"><p>AI in delivery is a force multiplier only when humans own the oracles, the sampling strategy, and the story you tell stakeholders.</p></blockquote><h3 class="blog-details__h3">Risks we surface early</h3><p>NSC assigns onboarding buddies outside the direct manager chain so newcomers can ask “dumb” questions without performance anxiety.</p><ul class="blog-details__list"><li>Define “ready for review” checklists</li><li>Rotate review partners weekly</li><li>Celebrate first production commits loudly</li></ul><p>Pairing across time zones works when sessions are recorded with consent and follow-up exercises reinforce what was live-coded.</p><p>Junior engineers in distributed teams need crisp tasks, visible code review norms, and mentors who narrate trade-offs instead of dropping “just fix it” comments.</p>";s:10:"post_title";s:47:"Mentoring Junior Engineers in Distributed Teams";s:12:"post_excerpt";s:292:"Mentoring Junior Engineers in Distributed Teams — Junior engineers in distributed teams need crisp tasks, visible code review norms, and mentors who narrate trade-offs instead of dropping “just fix it” comments. Pairing across time zones works when sessions are recorded with consent…";s:11:"post_status";s:7:"publish";s:14:"comment_status";s:4:"open";s:11:"ping_status";s:4:"open";s:13:"post_password";s:0:"";s:9:"post_name";s:47:"mentoring-junior-engineers-in-distributed-teams"